
    The BBSNet UK EchoMail Network
    ==============================

    BBSNet is the the first UK national network to operate in both the
    mail formats currently used on Bulletin Boards.

    BBSNet is available in FTSn (FidoNet) format and QWK style mail.  All
    other networks in the UK only operate in one of these formats, meaning
    that if your BBS uses the wrong style you cannot join and your callers
    get segragated from boards preferring the other format.

    BBSNet is available to ALL bulletin board systems, PC based, Amiga
    or Atari etc regardless of the software you use.

    For more information, please log on to our BBS to see these conferences
    in operation.  From there, by accessing the Questionnaire menu, you can
    also request a node number if you would like to join.

    BBSNet is Hosted by Cellular BBS, 01604-757777 / 464647 but can be
    seen in action on any of the boards listed in the file MEMBERS.NOD


    This network is completely free and we do not seek any form of cash 
    or subscription.

    This network is now available to absolutely ALL bulletin boards!


QWK Based Systems
=================

If you run a QWK based system such as Wildcat!, PCBoard, SpitFire etc.,
please look in the embedded archive:  QWK_BBS.ZIP  for useful batch
files to assist you with QWK mail transfers with the wcMAIL door on the
major hub systems listed below:

HUBS
====

You are free to approach any board carrying BBSNet/UFONet to obtain a feed,
(please see the nodelist) but these following systems, as well as Cellular
are known to carry the /full/ compliment Of BBSNet and UFONet echo's:


LONDON               Development System             (John Greenwood)
LONDON               Stairway to Heaven             (Shane Nolan)
LONDON               Atlantic Dream                 (Marc Fuller)
NOTTINGHAM           The Avenue                     (Alfie Geeson)
GLASGOW, Scotland    Flight of Fantasy              (Billy Connelly)
DUNDEE, SCOTLAND     ScotchMist                     (Mike Dailly)
GALLOWAY, SCOTLAND   Cyber Cottage                  (Jamie Wilson)
